D('kilogram',{
    etymology:{"origin":"kilo + gram","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[],"formationLogic":null,"mnemonic":null,"note":"kilogram 是质量单位，符号 kg；SI 前缀 kilo- 表示千，gram 来自法语 gramme 并经希腊语 gramma「小重量」而来。句中和 volume 对比以突出质量量纲。","source":"Etymonline — kilogram"},
    contexts:[{"domain":"实验 · 称重","senseId":"kilogram.s1","en":"Before the chemist compared the samples, she recorded each container’s mass in kilograms so that a small difference would not be confused with a difference in volume.","zh":"化学家比较样品前，先用千克记录每个容器的质量，以免把微小质量差误认为体积差。","structure":"Before the chemist compared the samples / she / recorded each container’s mass in kilograms / so that a small difference / would not be confused with a difference in volume.","grammar":"Before + 从句作时间状语；record A in units 表示按某单位记录；so that 引导目的从句。","rationale":"kilogram 是质量单位，符号 kg；SI 前缀 kilo- 表示千，gram 来自法语 gramme 并经希腊语 gramma「小重量」而来。句中和 volume 对比以突出质量量纲。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(2,'The recipe needs one kilogram of flour, so I weighed it before mixing.','食谱需要一公斤面粉，所以我在混合前称了重。')],mistakes:[m('The package weighs two kilograms, which is equal to two thousand kilograms.','The package weighs two kilograms, which is equal to two thousand grams.','1 kilogram 等于 1000 grams；两 kilogram 是 2000 grams，不是 2000 kilograms。')],quiz:[q('kilogram',1,1,'One kilogram is equal to?','one thousand grams','one hundred grams','one thousand metres','来源定义中 kilogram 是 1000 克的公制质量单位。'),q('kilogram',2,2,'A person who lost a kilogram has lost a unit of?','mass or weight','distance','temperature','来源第二义也指相当于一公斤的体重变化。'),q('kilogram',3,1,'Which abbreviation is given for kilogram?','kg','km','kW','来源明确给出 kg 作为 kilogram 的符号。'),q('kilogram',4,2,'Which sentence uses kilogram naturally?','The bag weighs two kilograms.','The road is two kilograms long.','The room is two kilograms wide.','kilogram 量质量，不量长度。')]});
D('kilometer',{
    etymology:{"origin":"kilo + meter","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[],"formationLogic":null,"mnemonic":null,"note":"kilometer（英式常写 kilometre）是1000米的长度单位；kilo- 表示千，meter 来自希腊语 metron「测量」。地图中的路线里程语境明确是长度。","source":"Etymonline — kilometer/kilometre"},
    contexts:[{"domain":"交通 · 距离","senseId":"kilometer.s1","en":"The trail map marks a spring every five kilometers, but hikers should still carry enough water because the final stretch climbs steadily away from the road.","zh":"步道地图每隔五公里标出一处泉水，但徒步者仍应带足饮水，因为最后一段会逐渐远离公路并持续爬升。","structure":"The trail map / marks a spring every five kilometers / but hikers should still carry enough water / because the final stretch climbs steadily / away from the road.","grammar":"every five kilometers 表示间隔距离；but 表示转折；because 引导原因从句。","rationale":"kilometer（英式常写 kilometre）是1000米的长度单位；kilo- 表示千，meter 来自希腊语 metron「测量」。地图中的路线里程语境明确是长度。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(2,'We walked for several kilometers before reaching the next village.','我们走了好几公里才到下一个村庄。')],mistakes:[m('The town is ten kilometers away, so it is a unit of mass.','The town is ten kilometers away, so it is a unit of length.','kilometer 是长度单位；距离不表示质量。')],quiz:[q('kilometer',1,1,'A kilometer is equal to?','one thousand metres','one thousand grams','one hundred kilometres','来源定义 kilometer 为 1000 米。'),q('kilometer',2,2,'“We walked for kilometers” describes?','a journey covering a long distance','a body weighing several units','a trip lasting several temperatures','第二义用 kilometer 表示路程中的一段距离。'),q('kilometer',3,1,'The symbol for kilometer given in the source is?','km','kg','mL','来源写明 kilometer 的符号是 km。'),q('kilometer',4,2,'Which spelling is the British variant?','kilometre','kilogramme','kilomitre','来源说明英式拼写为 kilometre。')]});
D('kin',{
    etymology:{"origin":"kin","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[],"formationLogic":null,"mnemonic":null,"note":"kin 指亲属、家人；next of kin 特指需要联系的最近亲属。英语 kin 源自古英语 cynn「家族、种族」，关联日耳曼语 *kunja- 及 PIE *gene-「生育、产生」。","source":"Etymonline — kin"},
    contexts:[{"domain":"家庭 · 亲属","senseId":"kin.s2","en":"When the patient could not speak for herself, the hospital called her next of kin, who had been listed on the emergency form as the person to contact.","zh":"患者无法亲自表达时，医院联系了她的最近亲属；紧急表格上登记此人为联系人。","structure":"When the patient could not speak for herself / the hospital / called her next of kin / who had been listed on the emergency form / as the person to contact.","grammar":"When 引导时间/情境从句；next of kin 是固定搭配；who 引导修饰 kin 联系人的定语从句。","rationale":"kin 指亲属、家人；next of kin 特指需要联系的最近亲属。英语 kin 源自古英语 cynn「家族、种族」，关联日耳曼语 *kunja- 及 PIE *gene-「生育、产生」。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(2,'The hospital asked her to name her next of kin in case of an emergency.','医院请她填写紧急情况下应通知的最近亲属。')],mistakes:[m('Please list your next of kins as the emergency contact.','Please list your next of kin as the emergency contact.','固定短语 next of kin 中 kin 不加复数 -s；删掉 s 即可。')],quiz:[q('kin',1,1,'A person’s kin are?','their family and relatives as a group','their co-workers at one office','their neighbors on one street','kin 泛指亲属或家人。'),q('kin',2,2,'On an emergency form, “next of kin” means?','the closest relative to contact','the next person in a queue','a distant friend with no family link','来源第二义指紧急时应通知的最近亲属。'),q('kin',3,1,'Which phrase is used in the source?','kith and kin','kin and kitchen','king and kinship','kith and kin 是来源列出的固定表达。'),q('kin',4,2,'The source notes that kin as a collective noun is generally?','uncountable and not pluralized with -s','always written as kins','a verb in the past tense','kin 通常作不可数集合名词。')]});
D('kind',{
    etymology:{"origin":"kind","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[],"formationLogic":null,"mnemonic":null,"note":"kind 在此是形容词「友善、体贴」，由主动提供物品和帮助的行为具体体现；be kind to someone 是常见搭配。此义历史上由「天生、自然」发展为对亲属般自然友好的态度。","source":"Etymonline — kind (adjective)"},
    contexts:[{"domain":"邻里 · 待人","senseId":"kind.s2","en":"Although the new tenant had arrived after the storm damaged her apartment, a kind neighbor brought over dry blankets and helped her call the landlord.","zh":"尽管新房客是在风暴损坏公寓后才搬来，一位热心的邻居还是送来干燥毯子，并帮她给房东打电话。","structure":"Although the new tenant had arrived after the storm damaged her apartment / a kind neighbor / brought over dry blankets / and helped her call the landlord.","grammar":"Although 引导让步从句；brought 与 helped 并列；help sb (to) do 中 to 可省略。","rationale":"kind 在此是形容词「友善、体贴」，由主动提供物品和帮助的行为具体体现；be kind to someone 是常见搭配。此义历史上由「天生、自然」发展为对亲属般自然友好的态度。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(2,'It was kind of the driver to wait until the older passenger was seated.','司机等到年长乘客坐稳后才开车，真是很体贴。'),ex(3,'The answer was kind of surprising, even though it was not completely unexpected.','这个答案有点令人惊讶，尽管并非完全出乎意料。')],mistakes:[m('What kinds of music do you like? “Jazz” is a kind of musical instruments.','What kind of music do you like? “Jazz” is a kind of music.','kind of 后单数名词 music；musical instruments 与回答的爵士乐类别不匹配。')],quiz:[q('kind',1,1,'In “What kind of music do you like?” kind means?','a type or category','a helpful attitude','a small degree','kind 作名词表示种类、类型。'),q('kind',2,2,'A kind neighbor is?','gentle, friendly, and willing to help','an exact category of furniture','slightly tired','kind 作形容词表示友好善良。'),q('kind',3,3,'In casual speech, “I am kind of tired” means?','I am somewhat tired','I am a type of tired person','I am being especially generous','kind of 可作口语副词，表示有点儿。'),q('kind',4,2,'Choose the standard pattern for treating someone well.','be kind to a stranger','be kind for a stranger','be kind at a stranger','来源提示 be kind to 后接人。')]});
D('kindergarten',{
    etymology:{"origin":"German Kinder + Garten","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[],"formationLogic":null,"mnemonic":null,"note":"kindergarten 是幼儿园，英语借自德语 Kinder-Garten，字面为「儿童的花园」，由德国教育家福禄贝尔于1840年命名，寓意培养幼儿成长的场所。","source":"Etymonline — kindergarten"},
    contexts:[{"domain":"教育 · 幼儿园","senseId":"kindergarten.s1","en":"Because the kindergarten closes before her shift ends, Mara arranged for her sister to collect the child and sign the pickup register each afternoon.","zh":"由于幼儿园在她下班前就关门，玛拉安排姐姐每天下午去接孩子并在接送登记簿上签字。","structure":"Because the kindergarten closes before her shift ends / Mara / arranged for her sister / to collect the child / and sign the pickup register each afternoon.","grammar":"Because 引导原因从句；arrange for someone to do 表示安排某人做事；两个不定式 collect 和 sign 并列。","rationale":"kindergarten 是幼儿园，英语借自德语 Kinder-Garten，字面为「儿童的花园」，由德国教育家福禄贝尔于1840年命名，寓意培养幼儿成长的场所。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(2,'In the United States, he starts kindergarten in September, the year before primary school.','在美国，他九月开始读小学前一年的学前班。')],mistakes:[m('Her son is in kindergarten, a class he will attend after finishing secondary school.','Her son is in kindergarten, a class he will attend before starting primary school.','kindergarten 面向年幼儿童、通常在小学前；中学后与此不符。')],quiz:[q('kindergarten',1,1,'A kindergarten is generally a school for?','very young children','university students','retired adults','来源第一义是接收约三到五岁儿童的学校。'),q('kindergarten',2,2,'In the U.S. source sense, kindergarten can mean?','the class year before primary school','the final year of high school','a university law department','第二义特指尤其在美国的小学前一年班级。'),q('kindergarten',3,1,'Which term does the source mention as common in British English?','nursery school','middle school','law school','来源提到英式英语也常说 nursery school。'),q('kindergarten',4,2,'The source notes that the age range for kindergarten?','varies by country and should not be assumed identical','is legally the same in every country','always begins after secondary school','来源提醒不同国家学制和年龄划分不同。')]});
D('kindle',{
    etymology:{"origin":"kindle","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[],"formationLogic":null,"mnemonic":null,"note":"kindle 作及物动词表示点燃、使开始燃烧。该词约1200年见于英语，可能来自古诺尔斯语 kynda 一类北日耳曼来源；更早词根不确定，也受到与 kindel「产下幼崽」相似形式影响。","source":"Etymonline — kindle"},
    contexts:[{"domain":"炉火 · 点燃","senseId":"kindle.s1","en":"Once the damp logs had dried beside the stove, Priya used thin kindling to kindle a small fire without pouring lighter fluid onto the wood.","zh":"潮湿的木柴在炉边烘干后，普莉娅用细小引火柴点起一小堆火，没有往木头上浇打火液。","structure":"Once the damp logs had dried beside the stove / Priya / used thin kindling / to kindle a small fire / without pouring lighter fluid onto the wood.","grammar":"Once 引导时间从句；use A to do 表示用 A 做某事；without + -ing 表示避免的行为。","rationale":"kindle 作及物动词表示点燃、使开始燃烧。该词约1200年见于英语，可能来自古诺尔斯语 kynda 一类北日耳曼来源；更早词根不确定，也受到与 kindel「产下幼崽」相似形式影响。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The dry twigs kindled quickly, giving the campers enough light to arrange the tent.','干树枝很快燃起，为露营者搭帐篷提供了足够的光亮。')],mistakes:[m('The speech kindled their hope, but it stirred no feeling in them.','The speech failed to kindle their hope, and it stirred no feeling in them.','kindle a feeling 与没有激起任何情感矛盾；补 failed to 使两部分一致。')],quiz:[q('kindle',1,1,'To kindle a fire is to?','start it burning','put it out completely','measure how warm it is','kindle 的第一义是点燃火。'),q('kindle',2,1,'A moving speech may kindle?','hope or another feeling','a kitchen appliance','a legal jurisdiction','kindle 也能比喻激起某种情感。'),q('kindle',3,1,'Which verb is listed as a near synonym?','ignite','ignore','kneel','来源将 ignite 列为 kindle 的近义词。'),q('kindle',4,1,'Which sentence uses the figurative sense?','The news kindled fresh interest in the project.','She kindled the wet blanket by folding it.','He kindled a kilometer into a kingdom.','激起人们对项目的新兴趣是 kindle 的比喻用法。')]});
D('kindly',{
    etymology:{"origin":"kind + -ly","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[],"formationLogic":null,"mnemonic":null,"note":"kindly 在此作副词，表示以礼貌、友善的方式提出请求；它由 kind + 副词后缀 -ly 构成。现代请求语中的 kindly 常显正式，有时语气较直接，需结合上下文理解。","source":"Etymonline — kindly (adverb)"},
    contexts:[{"domain":"沟通 · 礼貌请求","senseId":"kindly.s1","en":"The editor asked the author to kindly confirm the revised title by Friday, since the printer needed the final wording before producing the covers.","zh":"编辑请作者于周五前确认修改后的标题，因为印刷厂在制作封面前需要最终措辞。","structure":"The editor / asked the author / to kindly confirm the revised title by Friday / since the printer needed the final wording / before producing the covers.","grammar":"ask someone to do 是宾补结构；kindly 修饰 confirm，弱化请求语气；since 引导原因从句。","rationale":"kindly 在此作副词，表示以礼貌、友善的方式提出请求；它由 kind + 副词后缀 -ly 构成。现代请求语中的 kindly 常显正式，有时语气较直接，需结合上下文理解。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Would you kindly move your bag so the aisle stays clear?','请您把包挪一下，让过道保持畅通好吗？')],mistakes:[m('The clerk spoke kindly to the nervous child, using a warm and gentle voice.','The clerk spoke coldly to the nervous child, using a warm and gentle voice.','温和友善的语气符合 kindly；coldly 与后文冲突。')],quiz:[q('kindly',1,1,'If a nurse speaks kindly, she speaks?','in a friendly and considerate way','in a legally binding way','with no concern for the listener','kindly 作副词表示友好地、和善地。'),q('kindly',2,1,'In a request, “Would you kindly sit down?” kindly functions like?','please','perhaps','never','来源说明 kindly 也可作为礼貌请求用语。'),q('kindly',3,1,'Which sentence matches the source pattern?','Would you kindly wait here?','Would kindly you waiting here?','Would you kind sit here?','kindly 可放在礼貌请求中修饰动作。'),q('kindly',4,1,'Kindly is related to which adjective?','kind','king','keen','来源把 kind 列为 kindly 的词族成员。')]});
D('kindness',{
    etymology:{"origin":"kind + -ness","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"history":[],"formationLogic":null,"mnemonic":null,"note":"kindness 是抽象名词，表示友善、善意，由 kind 加名词后缀 -ness 构成。句中 volunteers 的具体帮助行为说明 kindness 的可观察表现。","source":"Etymonline — kindness"},
    contexts:[{"domain":"互助 · 善意","senseId":"kindness.s1","en":"What she remembered most was not the expensive equipment but the kindness of the volunteers who stayed late to help every family finish the application.","zh":"她记得最深的不是昂贵的设备，而是志愿者们留下来帮每个家庭完成申请的善意。","structure":"What she remembered most / was not the expensive equipment / but the kindness of the volunteers / who stayed late / to help every family finish the application.","grammar":"What 引导主语从句；not A but B 作对比；who 引导定语从句；help + 宾语 + 动词原形。","rationale":"kindness 是抽象名词，表示友善、善意，由 kind 加名词后缀 -ness 构成。句中 volunteers 的具体帮助行为说明 kindness 的可观察表现。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'A stranger showed kindness by helping the child find her lost parent.','一位陌生人帮孩子找到走失的家长，表现出了善意。')],mistakes:[m('Her kindness to the visitors was obvious: she mocked them and refused to help.','Her unkindness to the visitors was obvious: she mocked them and refused to help.','嘲笑并拒绝帮助体现 unkindness 而非 kindness；加 un- 是最小词形修正。')],quiz:[q('kindness',1,1,'Kindness may refer to?','the quality of being kind or a kind act','a legal right to judge a case','a unit of distance','来源兼含善良品质和友善行为两义。'),q('kindness',2,1,'Which phrase appears in the source entry?','an act of kindness','a kindness of kilometer','kindness on the jury','source lists an act of kindness。'),q('kindness',3,1,'The source allows kindness to be?','countable or uncountable','only a plural verb','an adjective with no noun use','来源说明该名词可数或不可数。'),q('kindness',4,1,'If someone shows kindness to strangers, they?','treat strangers in a friendly, helpful way','avoid every stranger without exception','appoint strangers to a jury','kindness 指友善和帮助行为。')]});
